# ---- 765 Government and Public Administration practicum (planning, project management, advocacy) ----
H("765.d.1.A",3,"A planner notes that wide sidewalks, bike lanes and nearby shops lead more residents to walk. This relates:","physical design to the functioning of the environment",["paint colors to weather","music to traffic laws","shoe sizes to roads"],"Design shapes how places work.")
H("765.d.1.A",4,"Adding crosswalks and lighting near a school mainly improves:","how safely people use the space",["the school colors","the lunch menu","the bell schedule"],"Design affects safety.")
H("765.d.1.B",3,"A city studies traffic counts and population growth to decide how many lanes a new road will need in 20 years. This analyzes data relative to:","present and future needs of a project",["last year's parade","a sports score","a menu price"],"Data guides planning.")
H("765.d.1.B",4,"Projected population growth is useful to planners because it helps them estimate:","future demand for services",["past weather","school colors","lunch prices"],"Forecasts drive capacity.")
H("765.d.1.C",3,"Before approving a new warehouse, a planner checks zoning rules, environmental laws and permit requirements. This assesses:","legal aspects of regulatory compliance in planning",["fashion rules","game rules","recipe rules"],"Plans must meet regulations.")
H("765.d.1.C",4,"A zoning ordinance controls:","how land in an area may be used",["who may vote","interest rates","school calendars"],"Zoning regulates land use.")
H("765.d.1.D",3,"A class reviews whether its mock public hearing followed the required notice, speaking time and recording rules. This evaluates a class activity with regard to:","regulations and procedures",["colors and fonts","songs and dances","menus and drinks"],"Check procedures were followed.")
H("765.d.1.D",4,"Public hearings usually require that residents receive:","advance notice and a chance to speak",["no information","secret agendas","no records"],"Notice and participation.")
H("765.d.1.E",3,"A student uses a map to mark parks, bus stops and flood zones and builds a chart showing the numbers. This performs:","mapping and graphic functions",["cooking steps","dance steps","sewing steps"],"Maps and graphics display data.")
H("765.d.1.E",4,"A map legend helps readers by:","explaining what the symbols mean",["hiding the data","changing the scale","removing borders"],"Legends decode symbols.")
H("765.d.1.F",3,"A planner predicts that a new rail line will change job access, clinic visits and social services in a neighborhood. This predicts the interaction between:","the economy, transportation, health and human services",["music, art and dance","weather, soil and rain","sports, snacks and games"],"Systems affect each other.")
H("765.d.1.F",4,"Better public transit can improve health outcomes by:","helping people reach clinics and jobs",["lengthening commutes","closing clinics","raising prices"],"Access to care and work.")
H("765.d.1.G",3,"A student attends a city council meeting and writes down which local, state and federal programs were discussed and how they affect residents. This documents:","observations about government programs",["a sports game","a movie plot","a cooking show"],"Documenting builds understanding.")
H("765.d.1.G",4,"Accurate notes from a public meeting should record:","who said what and which decisions were made",["only jokes","only the weather","only attendance fees"],"Capture facts and decisions.")
H("765.d.2.A",3,"A planning team lists new technologies, changing populations and funding limits as factors that will shape its work. This identifies:","emerging trends and barrier issues",["old holidays","school colors","past scores"],"Trends and barriers shape plans.")
H("765.d.2.A",4,"A barrier to implementing a city plan could be:","a lack of funding",["good weather","a clear map","public support"],"Funding is a common barrier.")
H("765.d.2.B",3,"When neighbors oppose a new bus route, the team practices negotiating and revising the route to reduce complaints. This practices:","problem-solving techniques to overcome barriers",["ignoring problems","blaming others","stopping all plans"],"Solve barriers with adaptation.")
H("765.d.2.B",4,"A good first step in solving a problem that blocks a plan is to:","identify the cause of the problem",["ignore it","assign blame","cancel the plan"],"Diagnose the cause.")
H("765.d.2.C",3,"A group compares making a plan through public votes, expert panels or small pilot tests and judges which fits its goals. This evaluates:","the style of strategies for achieving goals",["styles of clothing","styles of music","styles of art"],"Strategies differ in fit.")
H("765.d.2.C",4,"A pilot program lets planners test an idea:","on a small scale before a full rollout",["after it fails citywide","without any data","only on paper"],"Pilots reduce risk.")
H("765.d.3.A",3,"A student drafts a project proposal and gets the instructor's approval of the scope before starting. This initiates a project by:","securing approval of the project scope",["skipping the plan","ignoring the teacher","guessing at goals"],"Initiation defines and approves scope.")
H("765.d.3.A",4,"The initiation stage of a project usually produces:","a defined scope and approval to proceed",["a finished product","the final report","a closing party"],"Scope and approval.")
H("765.d.3.B",3,"A team lists tasks, assigns people, sets deadlines and estimates costs before starting work. This plans:","a project",["a lunch menu","a pep rally","a shopping trip only"],"Planning organizes tasks and schedule.")
H("765.d.3.B",4,"A project schedule helps a team by:","showing tasks, owners and deadlines",["hiding tasks","removing deadlines","adding confusion"],"Schedules coordinate work.")
H("765.d.3.C",3,"While building a public survey, a student answers a classmate's request for the question list and shares updates. This executes a project, including:","responding to requests for information",["ignoring teammates","hiding progress","stopping work"],"Execution includes communication.")
H("765.d.3.C",4,"During the execution phase, a team mainly:","carries out the planned tasks",["writes the proposal","cancels the schedule","celebrates success"],"Do the work.")
H("765.d.3.D",3,"A student tracks progress against the schedule, adjusts when a task slips and presents clear status updates to the class. This monitors and controls a project, including:","effective, cogent presentation of progress",["silent work","hidden results","random updates"],"Monitoring includes communicating status.")
H("765.d.3.D",4,"If a project task falls behind schedule, a manager should:","adjust the plan and communicate the change",["ignore the delay","blame a teammate","drop the project"],"Control means adapting.")
H("765.d.3.E",3,"At the end, a team delivers the final product, collects feedback, archives files and lists what it learned. This closes:","a project",["a window","a lunch","a sports season only"],"Closure includes lessons learned.")
H("765.d.3.E",4,"A lessons-learned review at project close helps teams:","improve future projects",["avoid reporting","delete records","hide mistakes"],"Learn for next time.")
H("765.d.3.F",3,"When a teammate is upset in a tense group meeting, the student stays calm, listens and keeps the discussion on track. This maintains:","professionalism in challenging situations",["rudeness","avoidance","anger"],"Stay calm and respectful.")
H("765.d.3.F",4,"In a heated one-on-one disagreement, the most professional approach is to:","listen and respond calmly",["shout","walk out without a word","spread rumors"],"Calm response.")
H("765.d.4.A",3,"A student pulls arguments and figures from a library database and trusted websites and judges how strong they are. This extracts and evaluates ideas from:","research library resources and online materials",["lunch menus","sports radio","social gossip"],"Evaluate sources.")
H("765.d.4.A",4,"A reliable online source for research is generally one that:","cites evidence and names its authors",["has no author","is anonymous","makes unsupported claims"],"Credibility check.")
H("765.d.4.B",3,"In a mock campaign class, students write questions, schedule sessions and role-play interviewing each other. This organizes and conducts:","practice interviews",["lunch breaks","school plays","gym drills"],"Practice builds interview skill.")
H("765.d.4.B",4,"Open-ended interview questions are useful because they:","invite detailed answers",["require yes or no","stop discussion","reduce information"],"Open questions elicit detail.")
H("765.d.4.C",3,"A student merges survey results, interview quotes and verified statistics into a report he designed himself. This compiles:","original data and reliable source information into an objective report",["rumors into a post","guesses into a chart","opinions into a slogan"],"Objective reports combine evidence.")
H("765.d.4.C",4,"An objective report should present information that is:","accurate and balanced",["one-sided","exaggerated","unverified"],"Objectivity matters.")
H("765.d.5.A",3,"A speaker appeals to logic, emotion and credibility, the classical patterns, and also uses modern storytelling. This analyzes and implements:","classical and modern patterns of rhetoric",["recipes","maps","scores"],"Rhetoric structures persuasion.")
H("765.d.5.A",4,"In rhetoric, an appeal to logic is called:","logos",["pathos","ethos","kairos"],"Logos = logic.")
H("765.d.5.B",3,"A debate team studies how different political, social and philosophical outlooks see the same issue. This analyzes:","differing political, social, ideological and philosophical perspectives",["identical views","a single viewpoint","no views"],"Perspectives differ.")
H("765.d.5.B",4,"Understanding multiple perspectives helps advocates:","anticipate counterarguments",["avoid persuasion","ignore opponents","avoid research"],"Know the other side.")
H("765.d.5.C",3,"A student checks whether a claim that crime fell 30% uses the right timeframe and source. This critiques:","facts and statistical claims for accuracy and relevance",["a poem's rhyme","a song's beat","a logo's color"],"Check claims.")
H("765.d.5.C",4,"Before sharing a statistic in a speech, a speaker should:","verify the source and context",["round it up","skip the source","assume it's true"],"Verify first.")
H("765.d.5.D",3,"A team removes a misleading photo and credits every source before handing out a campaign flyer. This ensures:","materials meet ethical standards",["materials look flashy","materials are longer","materials are cheaper"],"Ethical materials are honest and credited.")
H("765.d.5.D",4,"An ethical campaign flyer should avoid:","false or misleading claims",["credited sources","accurate facts","clear contact info"],"Don't mislead.")
H("765.d.6.A",3,"In a mock council meeting, a student maps what a landlord, a tenant group and the city each want and how their representatives speak for them. This compares:","interests of individuals, groups and their representatives",["breakfast items","bus routes","sports teams"],"Interests differ.")
H("765.d.6.A",4,"A constituent is best described as:","a person represented by an elected official",["a judge","a lobbyist","a clerk"],"Constituents are represented.")
H("765.d.6.B",3,"A class designs a project to help students understand neighbors with different backgrounds and beliefs. This explores options for:","promoting tolerance toward individuals and groups",["promoting conflict","ignoring differences","isolating groups"],"Tolerance supports civic life.")
H("765.d.6.B",4,"One way to promote tolerance in a community is to:","hold events where different groups meet and talk",["avoid contact","spread stereotypes","limit speech"],"Contact builds understanding.")
H("765.d.6.C",3,"Two classmates disagree about a project plan, so a neutral student helps both explain their view and find a compromise. This employs:","mediation techniques",["bullying techniques","avoidance techniques","gossip techniques"],"Mediation uses neutral facilitation.")
H("765.d.6.C",4,"A mediator is someone who:","helps parties reach agreement without taking sides",["decides who wins","joins one side","ends the talks"],"Neutral facilitator.")
H("765.d.6.D",3,"As a debate stalls, a student offers a middle option that gives both groups something they want. This suggests:","alternative proposals that keep discussions from collapsing",["ending talks","assigning blame","raising voices"],"Alternatives keep talks moving.")
H("765.d.6.D",4,"A compromise proposal usually:","gives each side part of what it wants",["gives one side everything","ends the discussion","ignores everyone"],"Compromise balances interests.")
H("765.d.6.E",3,"A city posts agendas, minutes and budgets online so residents can see how decisions are made. This discusses methods of:","openness in decision-making processes",["secrecy in planning","closed doors","hidden votes"],"Transparency builds trust.")
H("765.d.6.E",4,"Posting meeting minutes online increases:","public transparency",["secrecy","confusion","cost only"],"Open records.")
H("765.d.7.A",3,"A student builds a speech for a new youth center, using evidence, a clear request and a strong close. This delivers:","a compelling argument regarding a proposal",["a rambling story","a joke list","a silent poster"],"Compelling arguments use evidence and structure.")
H("765.d.7.A",4,"A compelling argument should include:","a clear claim supported by evidence",["only opinion","no structure","loud volume only"],"Claim + evidence.")
H("765.d.7.B",3,"A team creates a short video and slide deck to explain a proposed park project to council members. This creates:","effective media presentations and projects",["unreadable slides","blank posters","random clips"],"Media should inform clearly.")
H("765.d.7.B",4,"An effective slide for a council presentation should:","be clear, concise and focused on one idea",["be crowded with text","use tiny fonts","hide the main point"],"Clarity wins.")
H("765.d.7.C",3,"During a mock hearing, a student notices a skeptical audience and changes the pace and examples. This employs workplace skills to:","observe reactions and adjust accordingly",["ignore the audience","read faster","end the talk"],"Read the room.")
H("765.d.7.C",4,"If the audience looks confused during a presentation, the presenter should:","slow down and clarify",["speed up","stop speaking","insult them"],"Adjust to audience.")
H("765.d.7.D",3,"A volunteer coordinator recognizes effort, sets clear goals and asks for input to keep staff engaged. This evaluates and employs:","techniques for motivating staff",["ways to discourage staff","ways to ignore staff","ways to confuse staff"],"Motivation techniques.")
H("765.d.7.D",4,"Recognizing good work publicly is likely to:","increase staff motivation",["decrease morale","hide results","create conflict"],"Recognition motivates.")
H("765.d.7.E",3,"A team writes a checklist that requires disclosing conflicts of interest and crediting sources at each project step. This creates:","project steps for avoiding ethical pitfalls",["steps for avoiding work","steps for avoiding tasks","steps for hiding errors"],"Build ethics into process.")
H("765.d.7.E",4,"Disclosing a conflict of interest is a step that helps a team:","maintain trust and fairness",["hide decisions","speed up bias","create secrecy"],"Disclosure supports ethics.")

# ---- 766 National Security (Foreign Intelligence & Military practicum) ----
H("766.d.1.A",3,"A student leader sets clear goals, objectives and steps for a unit's simulated mission and checks them against the organization's mission. This explores and plans:","goals and objectives of an organization within a mission",["lunch plans","a playlist","a travel photo"],"Planning aligns goals with mission.")
H("766.d.1.A",4,"Objectives are most useful when they are:","specific and measurable",["vague","hidden","endless"],"SMART-style objectives.")
H("766.d.1.B",3,"A commander matches team members' skills to the tasks a mission requires, such as linguist, analyst or medic. This creates personnel assignments that:","align with job demands within a plan",["ignore skills","assign at random","avoid planning"],"Right person for the role.")
H("766.d.1.B",4,"Assigning people to tasks that match their training helps a unit:","perform more effectively",["lower morale","waste skills","cause delays"],"Fit boosts performance.")
H("766.d.1.C",3,"A student studies how performance reviews, standards and feedback are used to rate members in a service. This explores:","processes used to implement evaluation systems and standards",["methods for painting walls","how to cook","how to play games"],"Evaluation systems rely on standards.")
H("766.d.1.D",3,"A class reviews counseling, mentoring and training programs available to service members and how to use them well. This explores and reviews:","the usage of available counseling and training resources",["sports scores","music charts","menu plans"],"Resources support personnel.")
H("766.d.2.A",3,"A student charts what local police, state agencies, federal forces and international partners are allowed to do in a joint response. This identifies:","rules of engagement for agencies at different levels",["rules for board games","rules for cooking","rules for dances"],"ROE define limits of action.")
H("766.d.2.A",4,"Rules of engagement are meant to:","define when and how force may be used",["encourage random action","remove all limits","hide orders"],"ROE control force.")
H("766.d.2.B",3,"A class reads the Geneva Conventions and treaties on treatment of prisoners and civilians and judges how they apply to a mission. This evaluates:","U.S. and international laws, treaties and conventions applicable to missions",["local menu laws","school dress codes","traffic signs only"],"Law of armed conflict applies.")
H("766.d.2.B",4,"The Geneva Conventions mainly protect:","wounded soldiers, prisoners and civilians in war",["tourists","stock traders","sports fans"],"Humanitarian protections.")
H("766.d.2.C",3,"A trainer tests slides, videos and drills with trainees and revises the weak ones. This employs and evaluates:","effective training materials",["random handouts","confusing slides","unrelated videos"],"Test training materials.")
H("766.d.2.D",3,"After a scenario about treating a captured combatant, students talk through right and wrong choices. This facilitates group discussion of:","ethical issues raised by current events",["lunch choices","weather","fashion"],"Ethics discussions build judgment.")
H("766.d.2.E",3,"A student audits a mock operation's records to see if it followed military orders, international rules and agency procedures. This investigates:","compliance with procedures and laws",["compliance with fashion","compliance with cooking","compliance with art"],"Audits check compliance.")
H("766.d.2.F",3,"Using a new court ruling on surveillance, a student adjusts a sample plan to follow it. This applies:","current rulings and regulatory laws to appropriate situations",["old jokes","weather maps","sports rules"],"Apply current law.")
H("766.d.2.G",3,"In a case study, a student spots that an agent searched private records without a warrant. This recognizes and evaluates:","actions in violation of laws, rules and standards",["actions in sports","actions in dance","actions in games"],"Identify violations.")
H("766.d.2.G",4,"A search of private property without legal authority is an example of a:","violation of law and standards",["standard procedure","best practice","legal requirement"],"Warrantless search violates standards.")
H("766.d.3.A",3,"In a tabletop exercise, a team reads what its orders allow and forbid before acting. This explores:","the scope and limits of an assigned mission in a simulation",["the school bus route","the lunch hour","the music class"],"Know the scope.")
H("766.d.3.B",3,"A class assesses weather, local hostility, cultural friction and enemy capabilities in a simulated deployment. This evaluates:","physical, psychological, cultural and military threats",["fashion trends","ticket prices","soda flavors"],"Threat assessments are multi-dimensional.")
H("766.d.3.C",3,"Analysts study a rival government's statements and actions to judge what it wants. This defines:","the specific goals and intentions of foreign entities relevant to a mission",["a recipe","a weather forecast","a sports playbook"],"Intent analysis informs missions.")
H("766.d.3.D",3,"A student reviews terrain, climate, waterways and borders of a region where conflict could break out in the future. This analyzes:","physical characteristics of areas that could become battlegrounds",["colors of flags","menus","songs"],"Terrain matters.")
H("766.d.3.E",3,"A class reads about radar, satellites, drones and patrols used to watch land and sea. This explores methods used to direct:","ground and sea surveillance",["lunchroom supervision","playground games","bus pickup"],"Surveillance methods.")
H("766.d.3.F",3,"A signals trainee learns how radio traffic is picked up and decoded in lawful intelligence work. This explores methods used to:","intercept foreign military communications",["send birthday cards","sell phone plans","edit videos"],"Signals intelligence.")
H("766.d.3.G",3,"A joint exercise trains analysts to share findings with partner security agencies using secure channels. This explores methods to:","coordinate information with other national security agencies",["share recipes","send chain letters","post gossip"],"Interagency coordination.")
H("766.d.3.G",4,"Information sharing among security agencies should use:","approved secure channels",["public posts","personal email","casual chat"],"Protect classified data.")
H("766.d.4.A",3,"A student labels and logs documents, photos and call records so an analyst can see whether a threat is real. This organizes:","evidence to facilitate discovery of a potentially hostile nature",["party favors","sports gear","recipe cards"],"Organized evidence supports analysis.")
H("766.d.4.B",3,"A team reviews how an agency and the nation responded to a suspicious foreign act and what could be improved. This evaluates:","agency and national actions of a potentially hostile nature",["a school dance","lunch lines","a field trip"],"Evaluate responses.")
H("766.d.5.A",3,"A student drafts a plan for a drill that covers an attack as well as an accidental chemical leak. This creates plans for response to:","both hostile and unintended events",["only hostile events","only holidays","only weather"],"All-hazards planning.")
H("766.d.5.B",3,"A trainee lists masks, medical kits and communications gear needed for different emergencies. This explores and evaluates:","safety equipment and supplies needed for protection",["fashion gear","game consoles","lunch boxes"],"Equipment planning.")
H("766.d.5.C",3,"A class reviews threat reports to decide whether a risk is serious enough to warrant a response. This evaluates:","available intelligence information for determining threat level",["recipes","scoreboards","menus"],"Use intel to rate threats.")
H("766.d.5.D",3,"A student builds a dashboard that tracks public alerts and news feeds about threats. This creates:","a device or project for monitoring local and global intelligence",["a toy robot","a birthday card","a skateboard"],"Monitoring tools aid awareness.")
H("766.d.5.E",3,"A simulation team practices staying in contact with federal agencies when local networks fail. This discusses methods to:","maintain communications with federal agencies",["avoid contact","stay silent","delay reports"],"Communication continuity.")
H("766.d.5.F",3,"A class lists risks such as hacking, weak passwords and open ports and ways to protect a network. This identifies and reviews issues in:","the security and safety of network systems",["school lunch menus","sports uniforms","art supplies"],"Cybersecurity issues.")
H("766.d.6.A",3,"Before designing a course, trainers study what a mission requires and what skills trainees lack. This explores:","methods used to analyze missions for which training is needed",["menus for trainees","colors for classrooms","songs for drills"],"Needs analysis first.")
H("766.d.6.B",3,"A staff compares the results of an older classroom method with a newer simulation and decides what to keep. This plans and evaluates:","current and past training methods",["fashion trends","playlists","sports scores"],"Compare methods.")
H("766.d.6.C",3,"A student reviews how trainers use tests, observation checklists and performance drills to track trainees' progress. This reviews how agencies devise ways of:","evaluating trainee progress",["picking uniforms","planning parades","buying snacks"],"Evaluate trainees.")

H("766.d.1.C",4,"A rating system works fairly only if every member is judged against:","the same published standards",["each rater's mood","secret criteria","personal friendships"],"Fair evaluation uses common standards.")
H("766.d.1.D",4,"A service member who is struggling after a hard deployment could use:","available counseling and support resources",["avoiding help","hiding the problem","quitting training"],"Resources exist to help personnel.")
H("766.d.2.C",4,"After a drill, trainers ask students which slides confused them so they can:","revise the materials",["delete feedback","repeat the errors","skip future drills"],"Feedback improves materials.")
H("766.d.2.D",4,"A group discussion of an ethical dilemma works best when members:","listen to each view and give reasons",["interrupt","vote without talking","avoid the topic"],"Reasoned discussion builds judgment.")
H("766.d.2.E",4,"An inspector who finds that a unit skipped a required procedure should:","document the lapse and report it",["ignore it","change the records","blame a victim"],"Compliance checks require reporting.")
H("766.d.2.F",4,"When a new court ruling changes a rule, an agency should:","update its procedures to match the ruling",["keep old practice","ignore the court","delay for years"],"Follow current law.")
H("766.d.3.A",4,"Operating beyond the limits of an assigned mission can:","create legal and operational problems",["always help","never matter","earn automatic praise"],"Stay within scope.")
H("766.d.3.B",4,"Which is an example of a cultural threat to a mission?","misunderstanding local customs, which angers residents",["clear skies","a full moon","a quiet night"],"Cultural friction can derail a mission.")
H("766.d.3.C",4,"To judge a foreign government's intentions, analysts compare its stated goals with its:","actions and capabilities",["flag colors","anthem length","holiday dates"],"Words and actions both matter.")
H("766.d.3.D",4,"A planner studying a mountainous border region expects that terrain will mostly affect:","how forces can move and where they can hide",["the lunch menu","the school calendar","the language of songs"],"Terrain shapes movement.")
H("766.d.3.E",4,"Satellites help with surveillance because they can:","observe large areas from above",["only work indoors","only work at night","read private mail"],"Overhead imaging.")
H("766.d.3.F",4,"Intercepted communications are most valuable once they have been:","decoded and analyzed",["ignored","deleted","posted online"],"Raw intercepts need analysis.")
H("766.d.4.A",4,"Evidence helps an analyst only if it is:","labeled, dated and kept in order",["mixed up","unlabeled","lost"],"Chain and organization.")
H("766.d.4.B",4,"After a hostile act, a national review should ask:","what worked, what failed and what to change",["who to blame only","how to forget it","how to hide it"],"After-action review.")
H("766.d.5.A",4,"A good response plan for hostile and accidental events should include:","clear roles, steps and communication",["no assignments","only slogans","no timeline"],"All-hazards plans define roles.")
H("766.d.5.B",4,"Before a drill involving smoke, the team should check that it has:","masks and fire-safety gear",["extra snacks","spare costumes","party hats"],"Match gear to hazards.")
H("766.d.5.C",4,"A threat level is raised when intelligence shows a risk that is:","credible and imminent",["rumored","old","unrelated"],"Credible, imminent threats raise levels.")
H("766.d.5.D",4,"A monitoring dashboard is more useful when it pulls information from:","trusted and verified sources",["rumor sites","random posts","unknown accounts"],"Source quality matters.")
H("766.d.5.E",4,"If local networks fail in an emergency, teams should use:","backup communication such as radios",["no contact","guesswork","silence"],"Redundant comms.")
H("766.d.5.F",4,"A strong password policy helps protect a network by:","making unauthorized access harder",["inviting hackers","removing logins","sharing codes"],"Access control.")
H("766.d.6.A",4,"A training needs analysis identifies:","the gap between required and current skills",["the best snacks","the longest song","a school mascot"],"Gap analysis.")
H("766.d.6.B",4,"Before keeping a training method, a unit should check whether it:","produces results in trainees' performance",["costs more","looks old","sounds fancy"],"Evaluate results.")
H("766.d.6.C",4,"A fair way to track trainee progress is to use:","consistent tests and observation checklists",["opinions only","random choices","favoritism"],"Consistent measurement.")

